# Spec for tools/riscpkg.py: the lens profiles plug-in for Lumen.
Package: LumenLens
Section: Graphics
Priority: Optional
Licence: Free
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 0.4.0
Environment: any
Depends: Lumen (>= 0.0.38)
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-lumen
Description: Lens profiles for Lumen's Lens Correction
 The LumenLens plug-in gives Lumen's Lens Correction the profiles of
 1,533 lenses from the lensfun project's database, so Lumen can undo a
 lens's distortion, colour fringing and vignetting for the photo's focal
 length and aperture. Auto finds the lens from what the camera wrote in
 the file. It is only data, and goes into Lumen's Plugins directory,
 with its own guide.
Build-Map: !Lumen/Plugins/Lens -> Apps/Graphics/!Lumen/Plugins/Lens
Build-Notice: LumenLens, packaged for PackMan from the release zip on
 https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-lumen/releases
 .
 The lens data is from the lensfun database (https://lensfun.github.io),
 by the lensfun contributors, under the Creative Commons
 Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 licence, and is shared under the same
 licence. The plug-in's own text is under the MIT licence. The notices
 follow.
Build-Copyright: !Lumen/Plugins/Lens/Licence
